Remanufacturers inherit products with unknown condition histories, requiring expensive assessment before remanufacturing decisions. Continuous condition monitoring provides objective data enabling confident remanufacturing planning. Historical condition data enables predictive remanufacturing models improving quality and reducing costs.

Condition monitoring creates feedback loops where core condition information influences user behaviour. Users gain awareness of remaining core value and remanufacturing potential. Manufacturers gain real-world performance data improving next-generation design decisions.